  <div class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h2>I research patterns of intelligence and what's emerging.</h2>

    <div class="body-prose">
      <p>My name is Ken Davidson. I write under K Scott Davidson. I live in Far North Queensland — about as far from the centres of institutional thinking as you can get in Australia, which turns out to be a useful vantage point.</p>

      <p>For two decades I've worked with groups — thousands of people across corporate, community, and institutional settings — running processes that reliably demonstrate something most frameworks can't account for: that people have access to a quality of intelligence our default cognitive operating system can't produce. I've seen it too many times to dismiss and too consistently to call mystical. Something structural is going on. The work I do now is about naming that structure.</p>
    </div>

    <details>
      <summary><span>The framework, in brief</span><span class="plus"></span></summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p class="sub">Beyond Binary maps how human cognition arrested mid-development, leaving us running a survival-grade processor that sorts the world into categories but can't hold relationship, paradox, or emergence. Different traditions each worked out a piece of what the fuller cognitive suite looks like. None held the whole picture. The pattern is now visible.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span>Books &amp; current writing</span><span class="plus"></span></summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p class="sub">Author of the Beyond Binary trilogy: <em>Beyond Binary</em>, <em>Relational Intelligence</em>, and <em>Only Human</em>. The current book, <em>Unfinished</em>, reads our baseline anxiety as a structural signal from an interrupted cognitive installation — and asks what becomes possible when we recognise it.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

